# Ignore everything except ansible and docs
/*
!/ansible
!/docs
# docs/superpowers (design plans + specs) kept on-disk but intentionally untracked
/docs/superpowers/
!/scripts
!/evals
# Email-to-RSS Cloudflare Worker — tracked as a git submodule (see .gitmodules);
# its own .gitignore keeps wrangler.toml (KV ids) and node_modules local-only.
!/Email-to-RSS
!/.gitmodules
!prek.toml
!.ansible-lint
!/.shellcheckrc
!/.gitleaks.toml
!ansible.cfg
!/.vscode
!/.github
!/README.md
!/renovate.json
!/pyproject.toml
!/uv.lock
# The docs site config. Its build output (site/) needs no rule — the `/*` deny above
# already covers it, and scripts/docs/build_docs.py builds to a host path outside the repo.
!/mkdocs.yml
# Vale's config and the two custom rules. The deny-all above means these are invisible to
# git without an explicit allow — the same trap mkdocs.yml hit.
!/.vale.ini
!/styles
# ...but not the Google package. `vale sync` downloads it, prek's vale hook runs that sync
# whenever the directory is missing (so a fresh worktree self-provisions), and it
# is upstream content with its own release cadence. Pinning a vendored copy here would mean
# reviewing someone else's style diffs in this repo's history.
/styles/Google/
!/.python-version
!/PLANS.md
# The two community files GitHub looks for at the root. The deny-all above hid them once:
# they committed clean and simply were not in the tree afterwards.
!/LICENSE
!/SECURITY.md
# Track the SOPS-aware diff-driver attribute for secrets.yml. NB: rendering the
# decrypted diff also requires a per-machine `git config diff.sops.textconv`,
# which isn't set here — so this attribute is a no-op.
!/.gitattributes
# Make sure these are ignored
ansible/.env
ansible/.aws
ansible/.ansible
ansible/collections
ansible/roles/containers/code-server/templates/github
*.pyc
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
# Never commit private key material — defense-in-depth alongside the gitleaks
# pre-commit hook. These patterns have no leading slash, so they match in ANY
# directory, including the allowlisted ansible/ tree where a stray key would
# otherwise slip past the top-level /* deny rule.
keys.txt
*.agekey
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa
id_ed25519
!/CLAUDE.md
!/.claude
# Claude Code machine-local files live under the allowlisted .claude/ tree but are
# per-machine state (local settings/permissions, session buffers) — never commit them.
# The global ~/.config/git/ignore catches settings.local.json on this host; codify it
# in-repo too so a fresh clone is protected without relying on each machine's git config.
.claude/*.local.json
.claude/*.local.md
# Backup written by `audit-permissions.py --prune-dead` before it rewrites the local allowlist.
.claude/*.local.json.bak
# Permission-audit hook store — per-host runtime state written by
# .claude/hooks/log-permission.py; counts are machine-local by design.
.claude/logs/

# Ephemeral per-session git worktrees (.claude/worktrees/<name>). Session state, not repo
# content — and each is itself a git repo, so committing one adds a gitlink nothing can clone.
.claude/worktrees/

# Output of scripts/deploy_tools/backfill_staging_gate.py — one JSONL row per replayed commit,
# regenerated on every run. Local measurement, not repo content.
#
# It is ignored rather than merely untracked because the GitOps deployer reads
# `git status --porcelain` (gitops_deploy.py:998), which COUNTS untracked files, and treats a
# dirty tree as a healthy skip: the tick completes and writes last_run, so GitOps-Alive stays
# green while nothing fast-forwards. The file would park the primary checkout behind origin
# with every signal green: the deployer works exactly as designed and the only cause is the
# file existing.
.claude/staging-backfill.jsonl

# Claude Code writes a `tsconfig.json` into the root of each plugin it loads from a plugin
# directory, extending the `.claude-plugin/types/` scaffold it also writes. That scaffold
# ignores itself; the root file does not. Since dotfiles#797 sets CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS
# to `.claude/plugins/deck`, every session on the k3s nodes loads the deck mod from the
# primary checkout and recreates the file, which would park the GitOps deployer as above.
.claude/plugins/*/tsconfig.json
